payload:
  status: OPEN
  source: >-
    Proposed this session, grounded in loom/scanners/capability-map.js's real SYSTEMS map (the
    actual, checked list of which systems it scans: cortex, idearium, guardian, loom, ollama,
    eravos, clear-glass (x2), emerge, architect, copilot, bridge, nexus-healer) and
    nexus/autopilot.js's per-kernel definitions. Marked OPEN, not REAL — no real code anywhere
    constructs a persisted "system" record with these fields; SYSTEMS is a plain object literal, not
    a node file. Also found genuinely missing this pass: registered in KNOWN_TYPES and treated as
    real throughout this session's mapping, but no schema.system file was ever actually created
    until now.
  fields:
    id:
      type: string
      required: true
      description: real system name, matching capability-map.js's own SYSTEMS map key
    hasCapabilities:
      type: boolean
      required: false
      description: >-
        whether this system has a real registry-components.js — most do, some (versionium,
        intelligence) don't get scanned despite having one, a real confirmed gap this session found
    port:
      type: number
      required: false
      description: real port this system listens on, when it runs its own server
    spec:
      type: string
      required: false
      description: real path to this system's own .spec file, when one exists
